    "advanced_content_VYrEgr": {
      "type": "advanced-content",
      "blocks": {
        "image_nYKYrg": {
          "type": "image",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/yoga-restorative-cyndi-lee.webp",
            "link": "",
            "width": "33%",
            "alignment": "center"
          }
        },
        "liquid_3axGWg": {
          "type": "liquid",
          "settings": {
            "code": "<h3>Cyndi Lee\n</h3><p>Cyndi Lee has been teaching yoga since 1978, meditation since 1994, and leading teacher trainings since 1997. Founder of OM yoga, she is considered an authentic, fun and inspiring teacher who seamlessly integrates Buddhist teachings into asana classes.\n\n</p><p> Cyndi is the author of “Yoga Body, Buddha Mind” and “May I Be Happy: A Memoir of Love, Yoga, and Changing My Mind.” A practitioner of both Hatha Yoga and Buddhism, she has been been featured on ABC’s “Good Morning America” and The New York Times, and written for Real Simple, Self and Yoga Journal.\n</p>\n<p>\nCyndi’s guru is the Tibetan master, Gelek Rimpoche and she was an ordained as a Buddhist Chaplain by Roshi Joan Halifax. She holds a BFA and MFA in Dance from University of California, Irvine. Her yoga teachers include Judith Lasater, Rodney Yee, Patricia Walden, Sharon Gannon.\n</p>",
            "width": "66%",
            "alignment": "center"
          }
        }
      },
